                <pb facs="0798" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861b.01/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-29T18:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 29—10:16
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>117. My 106, March 23, 6[<hi rendition="#italic">9</hi>] p.m. Military attaché
                    today informed by War Office that troops which will occupy points mentioned on
                    mainland will be detached from force now based at Alexandrovsk in Russian half
                    of Sakhalin Island and that contrary to press reports troops on island will not
                    be proportionately increased.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
